  "content": {
    "id": "v2-c46b1-p29-practice-slot-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the normal to $y=x(x-2)^2$ where $x=3$, in general form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+7y-24=0$",
      "worked": "Expand:\n$$y=x(x^2-4x+4)=x^3-4x^2+4x$$\nPoint of tangency:\n$$\\begin{align*}y_1&=3(3-2)^2\\\\&=3\\end{align*}$$\nGradient function and tangent gradient:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=3x^2-8x+4\\\\m&=3(3)^2-8(3)+4\\\\&=7\\end{align*}$$\nGradient of the normal:\n$$m_{\\perp}=-\\frac17.$$\nEquation of the normal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-y_1&=m_{\\perp}(x-x_1)\\\\y-3&=-\\frac17(x-3)\\\\7y-21&=-x+3\\\\x+7y-24&=0\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
